      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "A positive integer with at least two identical digits is called a palindrome. On the other hand, an integer is called a natural number if it satisfies the conditions that it is either positive or zero. The number itself can be taken as the natural number or -a result obtained by subtracting an integer. In this sense, 0 is also a natural number, but we do not consider negative numbers to be natural numbers as stated in some sources. Therefore, we will only consider positive integers without negative signs in all of the discussions that follow.\nAnswer: \\boxed{11}",
