    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the smallest positive integer that is both an integer power of 11 and is not a palindrome, we need to analyze the properties of powers of 11. Palindromes are numbers that read the same backward as forward, such as 11, 101, 111, etc. Let's start by examining some powers of 11:\n\n- \\( 11^1 = 11 \\) (which is not a palindrome)\n- \\( 11^2 = 121 \\) (which is a palindrome)\n- \\( 11^3 = 1331 \\) (which is a palindrome)\n- \\( 11^4 = 14641 \\) (which is a palindrome)\n- \\( 11^5 = 161051 \\) (which is a palindrome)\n- \\( 11^6 = 1771561 \\) (which is a palindrome)\n- \\( 11^7 = 21435881 \\) (which is a palindrome)\n\nFrom this analysis, we can see that the only power of 11 that is not a palindrome is when the power is 1. Therefore, \\( 11^1 = 11 \\) is both a power of 11 and not a palindrome.\n\nThus, the smallest positive integer that is both an integer power of 11 and is not a palindrome is \\(\\boxed{11}\\).",
